# NASA GCN Kafka Credentials
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your credentials
# Get credentials at: https://gcn.nasa.gov/quickstart

# SECURITY NOTICE (Databricks Community Edition):
# Databricks Community Edition does not support Databricks Secrets.
# We recommend using Base64-encoded credentials for basic obfuscation.
# This is NOT encryption - it only prevents accidental exposure in logs.
# For production environments, use Databricks Secrets (requires paid workspace).

# Option 1: Base64-encoded credentials (RECOMMENDED)
# Use the provided script to encode your credentials:
#   python scripts/encode_credentials.py
# Then paste the output here:
GCN_CLIENT_ID_B64=your_base64_encoded_client_id_here
GCN_CLIENT_SECRET_B64=your_base64_encoded_client_secret_here

# Option 2: Plain-text credentials (NOT RECOMMENDED - for development only)
# GCN_CLIENT_ID=your_client_id_here
# GCN_CLIENT_SECRET=your_client_secret_here

# Note: The application will try Base64 versions first (_B64 suffix),
# then fall back to plain-text versions if Base64 not found.
